Requirement:
Hi Saran,

Following are the requirements for digital lending database operations. Please let us know if these are already implemented in liquibase pipeline or not. If not implemented request you to help on the same.
In the Digital Lending platform, we require the following capabilities to be supported through Liquibase-based database deployments to ensure controlled changes, rollback capability, and proper versioning.

1. Bulk Data Insert

Liquibase should support inserting bulk records into database tables as part of deployment scripts. This will help in onboarding configurations or master data required for multiple partners or journeys.

2. Backup Before Data Update

Before executing any update operations on existing records, the system should:

Take a backup of the existing data.
Perform the update operation.
Allow the restoration of the original data in case rollback is required.
3. Insert or Update JSON Configuration

For columns storing JSON configuration structures:

Liquibase should support inserting new JSON records.
If the record already exists:
Take a backup of the existing JSON structure.
Perform the update with the new JSON structure.
A mechanism should exist to restore the previous JSON configuration if required.
4. Stored Procedure Creation with Role Assignment

Liquibase should support:

Creation of new stored procedures.
Granting execution permissions to specific database roles as part of the same deployment.
5. Stored Procedure Update / Replacement with Backup

When modifying an existing stored procedure:

Take a backup of the current stored procedure definition.
Replace or update the stored procedure with the new version.
Maintain a rollback mechanism to restore the previous stored procedure if required.
6. Backup of Stored Procedures

Liquibase deployment should support:

Backing up individual stored procedures before modification.
Optionally creating a backup of all stored procedures prior to deployment for safety and audit purposes.


